WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.570
Hi, Jean! I'm Anna.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.550
I really feel like we’ve met before.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.950
Anyway, how can I help?

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.070
I want to see an interesting museum but I don’t know which one.

5
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.870
I can help with that.

6
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.270
I’ve lived in Washington, D.C. a long time.

7
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.950
I think I’ve seen all the museums.

8
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.550
Wow, thanks.

9
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.250
So, tell me, which museums are good?

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.910
Well, they are all good.

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.990
But they’re all different.

12
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:40.650
There are science museums and history museums and art and culture museums.

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.370
I want to see an unusual museum.

14
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.190
I like the Sculpture Garden.

15
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.770
Have you ever seen sculptures in a garden?

16
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.650
It is really artistic!

17
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.170
I have never seen a garden of sculptures!

18
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.490
I’ll write that on my list!

19
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:19.210
Have you been to the Museum of the American Indian?

20
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.370
I’ve visited that museum many times.

21
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.010
It is very peaceful.

22
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.410
I have always liked American Indian culture.

23
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.090
I’ll put that on my list.

24
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.750
Do you have any other suggestions?

25
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:40.270
Well, if you like plants, you can visit the U.S. Botanic Gardens.

26
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.970
It's very organic.

27
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.350
I have always loved plants.

28
00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.810
I’ll write that on my list, too!

29
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.370
Wow, you know so much about D.C.’s museums.

30
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.850
Well, I have lived here for over a year.

31
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:07.710
You’re so lucky to live in such a beautiful city filled with so many museums and a zoo!

32
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.170
What? D.C. has a zoo?

33
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.950
Yes, and it’s beautiful.

34
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.300
You’ve lived here for so long and you haven’t been to the zoo?

35
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.240
I've never been to D.C.’s zoo.

36
00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.560
I've never been to any zoos!

37
00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.080
You have never seen zoo animals?

38
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.740
I grew up on a farm, Jean.

39
00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.600
I've known farm animals my whole life.

40
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:51.560
But the zoo has lions and elephants and zebras!

41
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:57.980
If you have never seen a real, live elephant, you must.

42
00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.000
They are so majestic.

43
00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.360
I will.

44
00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.040
I will!

45
00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.220
There.

46
00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.360
I’ve written my own must-see zoo animal list!

47
00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.300
Have fun at the zoo and thanks, Anna!

48
00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.340
Have fun at the museums, Jean!

49
00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:17.740
And thank YOU!
